    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39872" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā^drĭfŏris</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		quattuor-fores, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>four-doored</i>, i.e. <i>having four
				doors</i> or <i>four doorways</i> (<i>openings</i>) (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nidi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 21, 24, § 74</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">januae,</span>”
				<i>having four leaves</i>, <i>divided crosswise</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					4, 6, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
